    A[Android POS / Business App] -->|amount, reference, intent| B[Vendor SDK / Terminal Adapter]  
    B -->|certified control channel| C[Payment Terminal / Certified Kernel]  
    C --> D[Card / Mobile Wallet]  
    C -->|encrypted/tokenized payment data| E[Acquirer / PSP]  
    E -->|result + token/reference| B  
    B -->|sanitized outcome| A  
  
    A -. never handles PAN/PIN if avoidable .-> C

Application signing also matters operationally. For managed payment terminals, vendors can impose their own app review and signing/deployment process. Adyen, for example, requires a signed APK before upload to its terminal-management environment and publishes terminal-specific application restrictions. citeturn825946search12turn825946search20

Recommended integration architecture, reliability and performance

The recommended design is a hexagonal/adapter architecture with one transport-independent terminal contract:

